Magic Markers really don't fit the legendary theme of the game, even if 
they are a tiny bit punny.

So instead go hunting for the giant flying cuttlefish (c) and apply each 
corpse for a bottle of ink.  Then while holding a quill of a harpy (h -- 
Watch your liver) in your primary hand and a bottle of ink in your off 
hand, apply the quill on the hide of a jackal to write most ordinary 
scrolls.  (Apply a knife, not a dagger, to skin corpses.)

The most powerful scrolls require the fireproof nature of a phoenix 
quill, the energy of dragon's blood and are best written on lich skin 
while blindfolded.

All classes except Barbarians, Rogues and Cave People start out with 
basic skill in literacy, but they'll need to train this up if they want 
to write the most powerful spells.

